Extension storage: LevelDB tables without compression, so run.sh can read TV Tools' settings.

run.sh reads TV Tools' start-up settings (Dark theme, GPU, Lite mode) by grepping the extension's chrome.storage
LevelDB. A saved value is plain text only while it is in the .log. The next start flushes it into a snappy-compressed
.ldb table, where the exact pattern no longer matches, and run.sh silently fell back to the default: a change held
for one start. Without compression the tables keep the JSON as written. This applies to every extension's value
store; they hold settings and lists of a few hundred KB, so the extra disk use is small.

diff -ru a/src/components/value_store/lazy_leveldb.cc b/src/components/value_store/lazy_leveldb.cc
--- a/src/components/value_store/lazy_leveldb.cc	2026-11-27 10:00:00
+++ b/src/components/value_store/lazy_leveldb.cc	2026-11-27 10:00:00
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@
     : db_path_(path) {
   open_options_.create_if_missing = true;
   open_options_.paranoid_checks = true;
+  open_options_.compression = leveldb::kNoCompression;

   read_options_.verify_checksums = true;

